--
-- Description
-- -----------
-- This tests the GEM modules response to HRESP not being OK in 10M or 
-- 100M mode operation.
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
-- -------------------
-- Receive several frames with hresp not ok set at various points in the RX DMA
-- operation. Check for correct status.
-- Transmit several frames with hresp not ok set at various points in the TX DMA
-- operation. Check for correct status.
--
-- Detailed Test Description
-- -------------------------
-- · Initialize GEM for 10 or 100 mode operation
-- · Check reset value of status registers.
-- · Enable the GEM for receive and transmit. Also, enable all interrupts.
--
-- · Receive a frame and get an hresp error in the data.
--   Check that this generates an hresp not ok interrupt.
-- · Receive a frame and get an hresp error in the first management write.
--   Check that this generates an hresp not ok interrupt.
-- · Receive a frame and get an hresp error in the second management write.
--   Check that this generates an hresp not ok interrupt.
-- · Receive a frame and get an hresp error in the management read for the next
--   buffer.
--   Check that this generates an hresp not ok interrupt and that the next frame
--   is dropped.
-- · Receive a correct frame.
-- · Check the statistics registers and ensure that the above operations were 
--   handled properly.
--
-- · Transmit a frame with an hresp error during data in the first buffer.
--   Check that this causes an underrun, hresp error is reported in the
--   interrupt and status register and that the tx halts.
-- · Transmit a frame with a hresp error in the first word of the second read
--   descriptor in the frame, check that it causes an underrun, hresp error is
--   reported in the interrupt and status register and that the tx halts.
-- · Transmit a frame with a hresp error in the second word of the first read
--   descriptor in the frame,  check that an hresp error & buffers exhausted is
--   reported in the interrupt and status register and that the tx halts.
-- · Transmit a frame with a hresp error in the second word of the second read
--   descriptor in the frame, check that it causes an underrun, hresp error is
--   reported in the interrupt and status register and that the tx halts.
-- · Re-transmit the frame. This time it sees a hresp error in the writeback
--   Check that it causes an underrun, hresp error is
--   reported in the interrupt and status register and that the tx halts.
-- · Re-transmit the frame. This time it sees a hresp error on the last
--   data phase of a burst (during the AHB DMA hold off state).
--   Check that it causes an underrun, hresp error is
--   reported in the interrupt and status register and that the tx halts.
-- · Re-transmit the frame. This time it completes successfully.
-- · Check the status and statistics registers and ensure that the above 
--   operations were handled properly.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

